---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | 3DPrintingCostCalc.com"
  description="Official Privacy Policy for 3DPrintingCostCalc.com. Learn about our 100% client-side zero-upload architecture, GDPR & CCPA compliance, and local storage standards."
  canonicalUrl="https://3dprintingcostcalc.com/privacy/"
  locale="en"
  showLanguageSelector={false}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", item: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy Policy", item: "/privacy/" },
  ]}
>
  <div
    class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16 space-y-10 text-slate-300"
  >
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="space-y-3 border-b border-white/10 pb-8">
      <div
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-mono font-semibold bg-emerald-950/60 text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-800/40"
      >
        <span
          class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 animate-pulse"
          aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>Zero-Upload Client-Side Guarantee</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400 font-mono">
        Last Updated: October 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Key Highlights Summary Card -->
    <div
      class="p-6 sm:p-7 rounded-2xl bg-[#0e1628] border border-cyan-500/30 shadow-xl space-y-4"
    >
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-cyan-400">
        <svg
          class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="2"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          aria-hidden="true"
        >
          <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path>
        </svg>
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-white">
          Summary of Our Core Privacy Principles
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ul
        class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300"
      >
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-2 bg-[#162035]/60 p-3 rounded-xl border border-white/5"
        >
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0">✓</span>
          <span
            ><strong>Zero File Uploads:</strong> 3D files (.stl, .3mf, .gcode, .obj)
            never leave your device and are processed purely in your browser's RAM.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-2 bg-[#162035]/60 p-3 rounded-xl border border-white/5"
        >
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0">✓</span>
          <span
            ><strong>No Account Needed:</strong> We do not ask for registration, passwords,
            email lists, or personal identity details.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-2 bg-[#162035]/60 p-3 rounded-xl border border-white/5"
        >
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0">✓</span>
          <span
            ><strong>Zero Tracking Cookies:</strong> No invasive third-party ad networks,
            tracking pixels, or cross-site tracking profiles.</span
          >
        </li>
        <li
          class="flex items-start gap-2 bg-[#162035]/60 p-3 rounded-xl border border-white/5"
        >
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0">✓</span>
          <span
            ><strong>We Never Sell Data:</strong> We have never sold, monetized, or
            shared personal data under CCPA/CPRA, and never will.</span
          >
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: Overview & Scope -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">01.</span>
        Overview &amp; Scope
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Welcome to <strong>3DPrintingCostCalc.com</strong> (&ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;our,&rdquo;
        &ldquo;us,&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Service&rdquo;). We provide modern engineering,
        economic estimation, and calculation tools for 3D printing enthusiasts, makers,
        print farms, and additive manufacturing businesses.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm">
        This Privacy Policy describes our practices regarding the information
        collected when you access or use our website. We believe user privacy is
        an essential human right. Because our service was engineered from the
        ground up as a stateless client-side web utility, our design
        fundamentally minimizes the collection and storage of any personal data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 2: Zero-Upload Technical Architecture -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">02.</span>
        Zero-Upload Client-Side Architecture (Technical Guarantee)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        When you drop, select, or parse a 3D model or slice file on
        3DPrintingCostCalc.com&mdash;including but not limited to <code
          >.stl</code
        > (ASCII/Binary), <code>.3mf</code> (XML/ZIP archives), <code
          >.gcode</code
        > / <code>.bgcode</code> toolpaths, or <code>.obj</code> geometries:
      </p>
      <div
        class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0e1628] border border-white/10 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono text-cyan-200"
      >
        <p>
          <strong>Browser-Native Processing:</strong> Files are read directly from
          your local file system via modern HTML5 JavaScript Web APIs (<code
            >FileReader</code
          >, <code>ArrayBuffer</code>, <code>DataView</code>, and Web Workers).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Zero Network Transmission:</strong> The raw geometric coordinates,
          vertex normals, polygon faces, layer heights, and extruder toolpaths are
          evaluated purely within your local device's volatile memory (RAM).
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Instant Ephemeral Purging:</strong> At no point are your CAD designs,
          commercial inventions, proprietary models, or G-code instructions transmitted
          across the Internet to our web servers, cloud storage, or any third party.
          Closing or refreshing your browser tab immediately frees and purges this
          memory.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3: Data We Do NOT Collect -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">03.</span>
        Information We Do NOT Collect
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        To eliminate privacy risks and safeguard commercial intellectual
        property, we deliberately refrain from collecting:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm pl-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Proprietary 3D Designs &amp; Files:</strong> We never capture or
          store your 3D models or G-code files.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Personal Identity Information:</strong> We do not collect names,
          physical addresses, telephone numbers, or government IDs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>User Accounts &amp; Passwords:</strong> There is no sign-up or login
          portal; the service requires zero credential management.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payment &amp; Billing Data:</strong> All calculation suites are
          100% free; we do not process credit cards, bank accounts, or crypto wallets.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Biometric or Sensitive Personal Data:</strong> No biometric, demographic,
          or special category data is ever collected.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4: Automated Technical Logging -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">04.</span>
        Technical Information Collected Automatically (Server Logs)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Like virtually all web applications, when your browser requests static
        assets (such as HTML pages, stylesheets, JavaScript scripts, or web
        fonts), standard web server logs receive technical telemetry from your
        HTTP request headers. This technical data includes:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm pl-2">
        <li>
          Internet Protocol (IP) address (used for geolocation estimation and
          DDoS mitigation)
        </li>
        <li>Browser type, engine, and version (User-Agent string)</li>
        <li>Operating system and device platform</li>
        <li>Referring webpage address and exit page timestamps</li>
        <li>HTTP status response codes and asset transfer sizes</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm">
        <strong>Legal Basis &amp; Purpose:</strong> This technical data is processed
        pursuant to our <em>legitimate interests</em> under GDPR Article 6(1)(f) to
        maintain network stability, prevent malicious automated scraping, defend against
        denial-of-service attacks, and troubleshoot 404 errors. Server logs are automatically
        rotated and purged on a regular scheduled basis.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5: Cookies & Local Storage -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">05.</span>
        Cookies &amp; Local Storage (localStorage) Policy
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        We do not use advertising cookies, profiling cookies, or third-party
        marketing trackers.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Our website uses the browser&rsquo;s built-in <code>localStorage</code> feature
        strictly for essential client-side personalization:
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table
          class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-white/10 rounded-xl overflow-hidden font-mono"
        >
          <thead class="bg-[#0e1628] text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 border-b border-white/10">Storage Key</th>
              <th class="p-3 border-b border-white/10">Category</th>
              <th class="p-3 border-b border-white/10"
                >Purpose &amp; Description</th
              >
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 bg-[#0a0f1d]">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-cyan-400 font-bold">theme</td>
              <td class="p-3">Functional / UX</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-300 font-sans"
                >Stores whether you selected &lsquo;dark&rsquo; or
                &lsquo;light&rsquo; mode to prevent screen flickering between
                visits.</td
              >
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 text-cyan-400 font-bold">printer_defaults</td>
              <td class="p-3">Functional / UX</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-slate-300 font-sans"
                >Caches your custom electricity cost rates, machine
                depreciation, or material cost presets so you do not need to
                retype them.</td
              >
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Because <code>localStorage</code> resides exclusively within your local browser,
        it is never transmitted in HTTP headers to any server. You can inspect or
        clear these values at any time using your browser&rsquo;s Developer Tools
        or Privacy Settings (&ldquo;Clear Site Data&rdquo;).
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 6: Third-Party Hosting & CDNs -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">06.</span>
        Content Delivery Networks &amp; Global Hosting
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Our website is statically generated and served globally via
        high-performance edge Content Delivery Networks (CDNs) and cloud hosting
        infrastructure. These infrastructure partners route static web assets
        securely and efficiently through globally distributed points of presence
        (PoPs). All data transferred across our network is enforced through
        256-bit Transport Layer Security (TLS / HTTPS).
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 7: GDPR & UK GDPR Compliance -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">07.</span>
        Your Rights Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR / UK GDPR)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), United Kingdom,
        or Switzerland, you possess statutory rights regarding your personal
        information under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 and the UK Data Protection
        Act:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 text-sm pl-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Right of Access (Art. 15):</strong> You have the right to request
          confirmation as to whether personal data concerning you is processed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Rectification (Art. 16):</strong> You may request correction
          of inaccurate personal data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong
            >Right to Erasure (&ldquo;Right to be Forgotten&rdquo;, Art. 17):</strong
          > You may request deletion of your personal data where applicable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Restriction of Processing (Art. 18):</strong> You may request
          limits on how data is handled.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Data Portability (Art. 20):</strong> You have the right
          to receive your personal data in a structured, machine-readable format.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Object (Art. 21):</strong> You may object at any time to
          processing based on legitimate interests.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Lodge a Complaint:</strong> You have the right to file
          a complaint with your local Data Protection Supervisory Authority.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 italic">
        Note: Because 3DPrintingCostCalc.com does not collect user accounts,
        email addresses, names, or identifiable 3D files, we typically hold zero
        personal data linked to your identity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 8: California Consumer Privacy Rights (CCPA / CPRA & CalOPPA) -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">08.</span>
        California Privacy Rights (CCPA / CPRA &amp; CalOPPA)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) as amended by the
        California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), California residents have specific
        statutory rights:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm pl-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Notice at Collection:</strong> We do not collect categories of consumer
          personal information other than transient IP addresses in server connection
          logs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Do Not Sell or Share Personal Information:</strong> We do not sell,
          rent, release, disclose, disseminate, or transfer consumer personal information
          for monetary or other valuable consideration.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We do not discriminate against
          any user who exercises their statutory privacy rights.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>&ldquo;Do Not Track&rdquo; Signals:</strong> We respect browser
          DNT and Global Privacy Control (GPC) headers. Because we do not track users
          across websites, our site behaves identically whether DNT is enabled or
          disabled.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 9: COPPA & Children's Privacy -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">09.</span>
        Children&rsquo;s Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Our website is intended for general audiences, STEM educators,
        engineers, and makers of all ages. We do not knowingly collect, request,
        or solicit personal information from children under the age of 13 (or
        under 16 in the European Union). If you believe a minor has somehow
        provided personal information to us, please contact us immediately, and
        we will take prompt action to remove any such records.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 10: External Links Disclaimer -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">10.</span>
        External Links &amp; Third-Party Services
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        Our educational guides, spool tare databases, and printer profiles may
        contain links to external third-party websites (such as hardware
        manufacturers, material datasheets, or open-source slicers). We have no
        control over and assume no responsibility for the content, privacy
        policies, or practices of any third-party websites. We encourage you to
        review the privacy policy of every website you visit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 11: Policy Modifications -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">11.</span>
        Modifications to this Privacy Policy
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        We may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in
        legal standards, web browser security standards, or our computational
        features. Any updates will be posted directly to this URL with an
        updated &ldquo;Last Updated&rdquo; timestamp at the top of the document.
        Your continued use of the website following any changes signifies your
        acceptance of the revised policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 12: Contact Us -->
    <section class="space-y-3 leading-relaxed border-t border-white/10 pt-8">
      <h2
        class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <span class="text-cyan-400 font-mono text-base">12.</span>
        Contacting Us Regarding Privacy
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm">
        If you have questions, inquiries, or legal concerns regarding this
        Privacy Policy or our client-side zero-upload data protection practices,
        please contact our team:
      </p>
      <div
        class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-[#0e1628] border border-white/10 inline-block space-y-1"
      >
        <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block font-mono"
          >Official Privacy &amp; Support Contact:</span
        >
        <a
          href="mailto:support@3dprintingcostcalc.com"
          class="text-base font-mono font-bold text-cyan-400 hover:underline"
        >
          support@3dprintingcostcalc.com
        </a>
        <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block"
          >Response Turnaround: Typically within 24 to 48 business hours.</span
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
